commit 1050ce6a4642917025dc1159f1b1b254336cdd6d

C03: the local YouTube player answers what is playing and stops on request, and a playback can precede the literal in one case (MUSIC1593)

«qué está sonando» and «pará la música» need a playback first, and with the local YouTube player the catalog could not see one: SMTC never observes mpv. The YouTube adapter now stands before the SMTC adapter and handles media.status and media.control while it has an active player — status reads the player's pause state over its IPC pipe and reports the title the playback receipt already named (authority local_youtube_player, source «BAXY YouTube (mpv)»); control stops the player and verifies its exit, or sets pause/play/toggle over IPC and reads it back; next/previous stand aside — and without an active player it stands aside entirely so the SMTC adapter answers as before. The composer accepts that authority as a media session. The conductor host gains `turn.playback-then` {cmd,text,caseId,followup,reviewDirectory}: the reviewed playback runs first (its proposal and completion emitted as the two «request» phases), then the follow-up runs as an ordinary turn whose terminal is the case's final; nothing follows a playback that did not complete.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


